  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With AV3, we can use the IsLocal Parameter to make a toggle that's local only. The problem is that objects enabled with it are still factored into the performance rank system for remote clients.\n\nAs an example, a HUD effect that requires a light for depth and is only enabled via the IsLocal AV3 parameter. The avatar will be kicked into \"poor\" ranking due to the light, even if it's local only. A remote client will never be affected by the light so there should be a way to entirely delete it (Similar to how safety settings does it) and skip it in ranking. \n\nA potential solution for this might be to have an object component that when placed on an object, flags it for deletion when IsLocal is false.  \n\nTL;DR - Extension of the \"IsLocal\" parameter for avatar performance ranking.",
